        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "Here is a **firm, professional, and demanding** version of your email that keeps the pressure on but avoids language that could hurt you legally:\n\n---\n\n**Subject: Immediate Request for Door Repair Quote – Ongoing Delay**\n\nDear Ms. Adam,\n\nI am writing to formally express my serious concern regarding the continued delay in receiving the door repair quote. It has now been over a month and a half, which is unreasonable for a matter that requires urgent attention.\n\nThis prolonged delay is significantly affecting my living conditions and creating unnecessary stress. A damaged door is a security and safety issue. I cannot leave my property unsecured, especially as I am preparing to return to the workforce. This situation should have been addressed promptly.\n\nI respectfully request that you provide the official repair quote immediately or confirm in writing:\n\n1. The contractor assigned  \n2. The date the quote was requested  \n3. The expected date of completion  \n\nIt does not take this long to obtain a simple repair estimate. The continued inaction gives the impression of neglect of responsibilities and lack of compliance with basic property management obligations.\n\nPlease treat this matter as urgent. If I do not receive a response within 48 hours, I will have to explore further action to ensure this matter is properly addressed.\n\nI expect a prompt and professional response.\n\nSincerely,  \nAmit Puri  \n\n---\n\nIf you'd like, I can also draft a **stronger legal-tone version** that references housing compliance obligations."
          ]
        },
